{
  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a systematic upward bias relative to true outcomes during volatile periods; apply a downward correction of approximately 1.5% to 2.0% on the forecasted value.",
    "When sentiment history shows a spike (e.g., +0.50) followed by neutral values, the model overestimates the continuation of that momentum; reduce the forecast trajectory to account for mean reversion.",
    "The model fails to capture intra-period volatility and assumes smooth linear growth; correct by introducing a variance buffer or reducing the slope of the forecast curve.",
    "Forecasts generated after a significant price spike (e.g., >2% daily gain) tend to be overly optimistic; apply a stronger negative correction factor when the previous day's close is significantly higher than the 18-day average.",
    "The model ignores the 'noise' inherent in EU ETS spot prices during transition periods; do not extrapolate short-term trends beyond 5 days without sentiment confirmation."
  ]
}
